K = 1048576, N = 4096: 1 <= M <= K (N/2 - 1) = 2146435072; the label bound Q M amount <= 2^62 - 1
every integer M in the range is admitted: nothing between the bounds is refused.

==============================================================================
C. The exchange of light between two lamps: every equal split is a fixed point
==============================================================================
flight age of 7 Links on a heading: 12 intervals (the engine's first click at tick 13 for a birth at tick 1)
unequal (32768, 8192), K = 4096, 600 intervals -> (29634, 11209); the engine's run: (29634, 11209)
unequal (32768, 8192), 6000 intervals -> (20806, 20035); the engine's run at 6000: see cavity.out
    t =     1: A  32760  B   8190  A - B  24570  total on the lamps 40950
    t =   100: A  32160  B   8680  A - B  23480  total on the lamps 40840
    t =   500: A  30089  B  10752  A - B  19337  total on the lamps 40841
    t =  1000: A  27989  B  12856  A - B  15133  total on the lamps 40845
    t =  2000: A  25066  B  15775  A - B   9291  total on the lamps 40841
    t =  3000: A  23331  B  17516  A - B   5815  total on the lamps 40847
    t =  4000: A  22127  B  18713  A - B   3414  total on the lamps 40840
    t =  5000: A  21295  B  19544  A - B   1751  total on the lamps 40839
    t =  6000: A  20806  B  20035  A - B    771  total on the lamps 40841
equal (20480, 20480), 6000 intervals -> (20420, 20420); the engine's run at 600: (20420, 20420)
the fixed points of the map (the content in transit, tau x s each way, held constant):
    total        2: split (1, 1) after 3000 -> (1, 1); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 1/4096)
    total       64: split (32, 32) after 3000 -> (32, 32); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 1/128)
    total     4096: split (2048, 2048) after 3000 -> (2042, 2042); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 1/2)
    total     8192: split (4096, 4096) after 3000 -> (4084, 4084); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 1)
    total    40960: split (20480, 20480) after 3000 -> (20420, 20420); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 5)
    total    65536: split (32768, 32768) after 3000 -> (32672, 32672); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 8)
    total   262144: split (131072, 131072) after 3000 -> (130689, 130689); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 32)
    total  1048582: split (524291, 524291) after 3000 -> (522759, 522759); FIXED (steady transit each way 12 x s, s = M / K = 524291/4096)
the map is linear in the contents (the cost per unit is the turn, M / K per self-creation;
    the click joins what was paid), so the total is conserved and any two contents relax to
    the equal split of their total: the set of fixed points is one per total, a continuum
    of every integer within the bounds of B. Nothing selects a content.

==============================================================================
D. Representability of nature's ratios on one integer grid (A10's test)
==============================================================================
    m_mu / m_e   = 206.7682830 +- 4.60e-06
    m_p / m_e    = 1836.1526734 +- 1.10e-07
    m_n / m_e    = 1838.6836617 +- 8.90e-07
    m_tau / m_e  = 3477.2300000 +- 2.30e-01
    m_pi+ / m_e  = 273.1324399 +- 3.52e-04
    m_pi0 / m_e  = 264.1430085 +- 9.78e-04
m_n / m_p = 1.001378419309366 (CODATA: 1.00137841931(49))
    smallest k (the electron's rung) fitting ['m_mu / m_e', 'm_p / m_e']: 13840; the rungs {'m_mu / m_e': 2861673, 'm_p / m_e': 25412353}
    smallest k (the electron's rung) fitting ['m_mu / m_e', 'm_p / m_e', 'm_n / m_e']: 18104; the rungs {'m_mu / m_e': 3743333, 'm_p / m_e': 33241708, 'm_n / m_e': 33287529}
    smallest k (the electron's rung) fitting ['m_mu / m_e', 'm_p / m_e', 'm_n / m_e', 'm_tau / m_e']: 18104; the rungs {'m_mu / m_e': 3743333, 'm_p / m_e': 33241708, 'm_n / m_e': 33287529, 'm_tau / m_e': 62951772}
    smallest k (the electron's rung) fitting ['m_mu / m_e', 'm_p / m_e', 'm_pi+ / m_e', 'm_pi0 / m_e']: 13840; the rungs {'m_mu / m_e': 2861673, 'm_p / m_e': 25412353, 'm_pi+ / m_e': 3780153, 'm_pi0 / m_e': 3655739}
    number of k below 3 000 000 fitting the muon and the proton: 989567
what this says: a grid fine enough (k of a few thousand) carries the measured ratios, as a
    fine grid carries any number; the test has no power unless a rule fixes k, and the law
    has none (section C). A10 was written for the superseded loop law and stays planned.

==============================================================================
E. The harmonic ladder a self-referential window would give (NOT the law) against nature
==============================================================================
    K = 1048576, N = 64, round trip tau = 24: rung spacing K N / tau = 8388608/3
    K = 1048576, N = 64, round trip tau = 240: rung spacing K N / tau = 4194304/15
    K = 1073741824, N = 64, round trip tau = 24: rung spacing K N / tau = 8589934592/3
    R = (m_p - m_e) / (m_mu - m_e) = 8.918540052 +- 2.0e-07
    smallest p / q within the uncertainty: (27371, 3069); rungs from the electron to the muon: 3069
    leptons nature shows between the electron and the muon: 0 (the next charged lepton is the tau, at 3477)
verdict of E: the only ladder a clock resonance can give is harmonic (equally spaced in the
    content), and a harmonic ladder that carries the electron, the muon and the proton has
    3068 unseen rungs between the electron and the muon; refuted by the spectrum.

==============================================================================
F. What the law says about composites (no mass defect) against nature
==============================================================================
    deuteron: the law's content m_p + ... = 3674.83634 m_e exactly (a free ray carries no content); nature 3670.48297 m_e; the law is above by 4.353 m_e = 2.225 MeV (0.119 %)
    alpha: the law's content m_p + ... = 7349.67267 m_e exactly (a free ray carries no content); nature 7294.29954 m_e; the law is above by 55.373 m_e = 28.296 MeV (0.759 %)
    the register's integers 1836 and 1839 (series I, H): m_n / m_p = 1839 / 1836 = 1.0016340 against nature's 1.0013784: an input, and rounded
    the muon (207), the tau (3477), the pions: catalog values; the law has no rung for any of them.
